  "name": "Jikong yue (Confucian temple ritual music)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Ceremonial music of the sacrifice to Confucius, performed at the Temple of Confucius in Qufu, Shandong, at the Taipei Confucius Temple and elsewhere, descended from the court yayue repertory of hymns sung at the ceremony. Slow hymn lines, one long note per syllable, are sung over ritual instruments of the 'eight sounds', among them bronze bells, stone chimes, qin and se zithers, xiao pipes, xun ocarina, sheng and drums, while dancers perform the ritual dance; the stone chimes and se have no card here.",
